# jev-diffusion (Rust)

> Rust bindings around the JEV-Diffusion Python engine.

JEV-Diffusion is substrate-segmented image description via JEV + LLMs as GAN.
No actual image generator needed.

## Use (via Python engine)

```rust
use jev_diffusion::{JevDiffusion, call_jev, call_qwen};

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    // Direct Rust API to JEV and Qwen
    let jev_resp = call_jev(
        "a serene sunset",
        serde_json::json!({
            "mood": {
                "type": "choice",
                "instructions": "What mood?",
                "criteria": {"serene": "calm", "dramatic": "intense"}
            }
        }),
        &std::env::var("TYPESAFEAI_KEY").unwrap(),
    ).await.unwrap();

    let qwen_resp = call_qwen(
        "Describe a sunset",
        &std::env::var("DEEPINFRA_TOKEN").unwrap(),
        1000,
    ).await.unwrap();
}
```

